    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1FB__STAT" kindref="compound">FB_STAT</ref> register bit definitions. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>General feedback and status information. <simplesect kind="warning"><para><ref refid="namespacetle92466ed_1_1FB__STAT" kindref="compound">FB_STAT</ref> is a <bold>22-bit</bold> reply register. <computeroutput>INIT_DONE</computeroutput> (21) and <computeroutput>SPI_WD_ERR</computeroutput> (20) sit above bit 15, so a caller that narrows the <computeroutput>ReadRegister</computeroutput> result to <computeroutput>uint16_t</computeroutput> silently loses them and reads <computeroutput>INIT_DONE</computeroutput> as 0 forever. Keep these masks 32-bit.</para>
</simplesect>
Bit positions per datasheet Rev. 1.2 (2022-02-01) §5.3.2.21, Table 23. Reset value is 0x200638 — note <computeroutput>INIT_DONE</computeroutput> is set out of reset. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
    <location file="inc/tle92466ed_registers.hpp" line="538" column="1"/>
